-- title:
--   Affine chart at a supersingular place over small constants
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $q$ is a prime with $5\le q$, $M'$ is a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$, and $A$ is a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ lies in the non-units of $A$; write $\kappa=$ `ResidueField A`.
--
--   *Supersingular place data.* $W$ is a finite set of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` (the intermediate field of `LaurentSeries κ` over $\kappa$ generated by the $q$-expansions `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`) over $\kappa$, and `hW` says that $W$ consists exactly of the supersingular places `ssPlaces q M' κ`, that is of those places $w$ which are rational (the structure map $\kappa\to$ `w.ResidueField` is surjective), which satisfy `IsAffineGeomPlace κ M'`, and whose value `w.evalAt (jGeomGen κ M')` lies in `ssJSet q κ`. A place here is a valuation subring of the function field containing the image of the base field, distinct from the whole field, and a principal ideal ring; `ord` is the associated normalised valuation, and `evalAt f` is the element of the base field representing the residue of $f$ when $f$ is in the valuation subring, and $0$ otherwise. The hypothesis `hle` asserts the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` $\le$ `fieldBar q M'` of the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the full-level-$M'$ modular function field into the base change to $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of the function field of $X_H$ at level $q^2M'$, for $H=$ `levelH q M'` the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$.
--
--   *Reduction data.* $R_0$ is a `ConstantReduction` of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`: a valuation subring `R₀.integers`, a surjective ring homomorphism `R₀.residue` onto `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` with kernel the maximal ideal of `R₀.integers`, a map `R₀.placeMap` on places, compatibility of membership and of residues with $A\to\kappa$, the existence for each nonzero $f$ of a constant $c$ with $c\cdot f$ integral of nonzero residue, and preservation of degrees and of divisors. The hypothesis `hR₀` requires that the reduction be computed coefficientwise: for every Laurent series $y$ over $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image lies in `R₀.integers` and its `R₀.residue` is, as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, the coefficientwise reduction of $y$. Finally $s$ is a chosen element of $W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   *Small-constants data.* $k_0$ is an intermediate field of $\mathbb Q\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and $\pi_0\in k_0$ an element lying in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); the hypothesis `hκ` requires $A=(A\cap k_0)+\mathfrak m_A$, in the form: every $a\in A$ admits $c\in k_0\cap A$ with $a-c$ in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   *Auxiliary prime and uniformiser.* $\ell$ is a prime with $3\le\ell$, $\ell\ne q$ and $\ell\nmid M'$; $\zeta_0\in k_0$ is a primitive $q\ell$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$; and $\varpi_t\in k_0$ lies in $A$ and satisfies $\varpi_t^{\,q^2-1}=q\cdot u$ for some unit $u$ of $A$.
--
--   *Base layer.* $K_b$ is an intermediate field of $k_0\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $K_b=\bot$, $A_b$ is a valuation subring of $K_b$ whose members are exactly the elements of $K_b$ lying in $A$, and $\varpi_b$ is a nonzero element of $A_b$ generating the maximal ideal of $A_b$.
--
--   The conclusion is stated with $k_0$ acting on `fieldBar q M'` through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. It asserts the existence of an intermediate field $F_0$ of `fieldBar q M'` over $k_0$ and a valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ with the following properties.
--
--   (1) The join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $F_0$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   (2) For $x\in k_0$: $x\in A$ if and only if the image of $x$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$.
--
--   (3) $W_0$ is a discrete valuation ring.
--
--   (4) The image of $\pi_0$ in $F_0$ lies in $W_0$ and generates the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (5) There is $t\in W_0$ which is residually transcendental in the following sense: for every polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$, if $p(t)$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, then every coefficient of $p$ has image in $W_0$ lying in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (6) $W_0$ lies over the place $s$ on functions regular away from the cusps: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in `R₀.integers`, if that image has non-negative order at every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ at which the image of $j_q$ has non-negative order, and if `R₀.residue` of it lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $F_0$, the resulting element of $F_0$ lies in $W_0$, and for every $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals `s.evalAt` of `R₀.residue` of $g$, the difference of that element and the image of $c$ lies in $W_0$ and in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   (7) Level stability: for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` (a primitive $q$-th root of unity in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$) and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')\subset\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, the automorphism `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` of `fieldBar q M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ maps $F_0$ into itself, and for $f\in F_0$ with image again in $F_0$, $f$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if its image does.
--
--   (8) Linear disjointness: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0\subset\overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every family $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$, and every family $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to$ `fieldBar q M'` with all $a_i$ in the join of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$ with $F_0$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$.
--
--   (9) An affine chart: there are a subring $B$ of `fieldBar q M'` and an $A_b$-algebra structure on $B$ such that
--
--   (a) the structure map sends $a\in A_b$ to the image of $a$ under $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`;
--
--   (b) $B$ is contained in the join $L$ of the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K_b$ with $F_0$;
--
--   (c) every element of $L$ is a ratio $g/h$ with $g,h\in B$, $h\neq0$, so $L$ is the fraction field of $B$;
--
--   (d) $B$ is formally smooth and of finite presentation over $A_b$;
--
--   (e) $B/\varpi_bB$ has Krull dimension at most $1$;
--
--   (f) every element of $B$ lies in $F_0$ and in $W_0$;
--
--   (g) the image of $\varpi_b$ in $B$ is prime;
--
--   (h) $W_0$ is the localisation of $B$ at that prime: $f\in F_0$ lies in $W_0$ if and only if $f=g/h$ with $g,h\in B$ and the image of $\varpi_b$ not dividing $h$;
--
--   (i) the image of $j_q$ in `fieldBar q M'` under the inclusion given by `hle` lies in $B$;
--
--   (j) $B$ is stable under `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ` for every $\zeta$ in `Idx q` and every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$;
--
--   (k) the special fibre is an affine quotient Drinfeld curve: for every $\mathbb F_{q^2}$-algebra structure on $\kappa$, every proof that [`DrinfeldCurve.CoordRing q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L21) (the quotient of the polynomial ring in two variables over $\kappa$ by the ideal generated by `drinfeldPoly q κ - 1`) is a domain, and every $\zeta$ in `Idx q`, there exist a subgroup $C_s$ of the group of $(q+1)$-st roots of unity in `GaloisField q 2` and a ring homomorphism $\rho$ from $B$ to [`DrinfeldCurve.quotField q κ Cs`](def/ModularCurve_FullLevelSemistableCoveringW2.html#L32) (the fixed field, inside the fraction field `drinfeldFunctionField q κ` of the coordinate ring, of the subgroup generated by the operators `hFunctionFieldAction q κ ⟨(1, ζ'), _⟩` for $\zeta'\in C_s$) such that: the cardinality of $C_s$ is $2\cdot$`placeWidthChar q M' s`; the kernel of $\rho$ is the ideal generated by the image of $\varpi_b$; $\rho$ composed with the structure map $A_b\to B$ is reduction $A\to\kappa$ followed by $\kappa\to$ `quotField q κ Cs`; every element of `quotField q κ Cs` is a ratio $\rho(g)/\rho(h)$ with $g,h\in B$ and $\rho(h)\neq0$; an element $z$ of `quotField q κ Cs` lies in the range of $\rho$ if and only if, viewed in `drinfeldFunctionField q κ`, it lies in the image of the coordinate ring; and $\rho$ is equivariant, in the sense that for every $\gamma\in\Gamma_0(M')$ such that the pair $(\mathrm{redQ}\,q\,\gamma,1)$ of the reduction of $\gamma$ modulo $q$ and the unit $1$ lies in [`DrinfeldCurve.hSubgroup q`](def/DrinfeldCurve_CoordRing.html#L276), and every $f\in B$ with `levelAutBar q M' ζ γ⁻¹ f` again in $B$, the image under $\rho$ of the latter equals the action of that pair through [`DrinfeldCurve.hFunctionFieldAction q κ`](def/DrinfeldCurve_FunctionField.html#L16) on the image of $\rho(f)$ in `drinfeldFunctionField q κ`.
--
--   No description of $F_0$ in terms of the $k_0$-rationality of Laurent coefficients is part of the conclusion; $F_0$ and $W_0$ are constrained only by (1)–(9).
--
--   This is the ring-theoretic half of the descent to small constants of a regular model of the full-level modular curve of level $q^2M'$ at a supersingular point: it produces the field of definition $F_0$ with its discrete valuation ring $W_0$ over the chosen supersingular place $s$, together with one smooth affine $A_b$-curve $\operatorname{Spec} B$ whose generic fibre has function field $k_0\cdot F_0$ and whose special fibre is the quotient by $C_s$ of the affine Drinfeld (Deligne–Lusztig) curve over the residue field. It is used by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_klevel_supersingularDVR_baseSmoothPointStalks), which converts the chart into statements about local rings at points of the base.
